	</div>



</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><a href="https://www.mfah.org/exhibitions/pipilotti-rist-pixel-forest-and-worry-will-vanish" target="_blank"><strong>Worry Will Vanish</strong></a> is a corner projection with a lyrical, resonantly textured soundtrack by musician Anders Guggisberg, who has worked with <strong>Rist</strong> on numerous projects. <strong>Rist</strong>’s panoramic sequences chart a dreamlike journey through the natural landscape, the human body, and the heavens. Visitors are invited to experience these two works of art in two different ways. For <strong>Pixel Forest</strong>, take a stroll through the installation, which the artist describes as “a digital image that has exploded in space.” As you watch <strong>Worry Will Vanish</strong>, recline on pillows and relax, losing yourself in<strong> Rist</strong>’s universe.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img decoding="async" class="alignnone wp-image-41608 size-full" title="Pipilotti Rist: Pixel Forest and Worry Will Vanish" src="http://www.itsliquid.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/Pipilotti_Rist_003.jpg" alt="Pipilotti Rist: Pixel Forest and Worry Will Vanish" width="648" height="486" srcset="https://www.itsliquid.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/Pipilotti_Rist_003.jpg 648w, https://www.itsliquid.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/Pipilotti_Rist_003-300x225.jpg 300w, https://www.itsliquid.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/Pipilotti_Rist_003-624x468.jpg 624w" sizes="(max-width: 648px) 100vw, 648px" /></p>
<p><sub>Image courtesy of The Museum of Fine Arts</sub></p>
